{
  "$schema": "../../catalog/skill.spec.schema.json",
  "id": "azuresql-db-feedback",
  "domain": "azure-sql-database-container",
  "value": [
    "not-in-training-data"
  ],
  "correction": "Told that something did not work, an agent says \"file an issue\" and leaves the user to it. A skill problem and a product problem use different templates, the report needs context the agent already has, and secrets in a pasted connection string would become world-readable, so the report is built, redacted, and never submitted without explicit confirmation.",
  "posture": [
    "read"
  ],
  "maturity": "preview",
  "value_declaration": {
    "rationale": "This skill's kernel is project-specific routing: which of two issue templates a report belongs in and where it is filed. The Azure SQL Database container is a gated private preview and the image is not publicly available, so no model has training data on the product, and the arm of a two-arm value run that ran without this skill would fail for the least interesting reason available: it has never heard of the thing. Running that measurement across all seventeen container skills would spend around a thousand model requests to re-establish what the product's release status already establishes. Carlos Robles accepted value for this collection on 2026-09-04 on this written argument instead. THIS IS A DECLARATION AND NOT A MEASUREMENT, and nothing may report it as one. The argument reaches only the container-specific corrections listed in covers, which are the ones no training data contains. It does not reach redacting a pasted connection string, asking before submitting, and how to write a good bug report, which is ordinary material an ordinary model already handles, and whether this skill improves an answer there is unmeasured and stays unmeasured. The argument ends when the Azure SQL Database container reaches Public Preview: training data begins to contain the product, the premise that nothing could know it stops being true, and this skill has to be measured or demoted. Its maturity is decided by its probes and not by this argument. This skill has no engine surface at all, so it declares validation.target of none and is judged on the instrument that does fit it, which is whether the short link its reports travel on still resolves to the template it names.",
    "covers": [
      "the two distinct issue templates this product uses and the test that decides between them, which exists only in this project",
      "the aka.ms destination a report is filed to, which is project-specific and in no training data",
      "which facts the agent already holds and the user does not, for this product specifically: the image tag, the host and the runtime"
    ],
    "does_not_cover": [
      "redacting secrets from a pasted connection string, and the practice of confirming before submitting anything",
      "how to write a clear bug report, which is ordinary material"
    ],
    "decided_by": "Carlos Robles",
    "decided_on": "2026-09-04",
    "expires_when": "the-container-reaches-public-preview"
  },
  "applies_to": [
    "azure-sql-db-container"
  ],
  "validation": {
    "target": "none",
    "probes": [
      {
        "cmd": "sh -c 'curl -fsS -o /dev/null -w \"%{redirect_url}\" \"https://aka.ms/sql-agent-skills-feedback?title=PROBE&labels=PROBE\" | grep -q \"issues/new?template=skill_feedback.yml$\"'",
        "where": "host",
        "expect": {
          "succeeds": true
        },
        "why": "The one claim in this skill an engine of any kind can settle, and the reason it is worth a probe is that being wrong about it fails silently: the user opens a form, sees it empty, and has no way to know a filled report was dropped on the way. Measured on 2026-09-04, aka.ms/sql-agent-skills-feedback answers 301 to https://github.com/microsoft/azure-sql-database-container/issues/new?template=skill_feedback.yml, with title and labels gone. The grep anchors on the end of the redirect target, so the probe fails both if a query string survives, which would mean the skill's prohibition is now unnecessary, and if the short link is ever repointed at a different template, which would misroute every report this skill files. It runs on the host because it is a link, not a database: nothing about it involves the engine, and the container has no reason to carry curl."
      }
    ]
  },
  "triggering": {
    "explicit": [
      "Use the azuresql-db-feedback skill"
    ],
    "implicit": [
      "the skill told my agent the wrong thing, how do I report it"
    ],
    "negative": [
      "set up a local PostgreSQL database with docker compose",
      "provision an Azure SQL Database in my subscription",
      "connect to SQL Server on my company network"
    ]
  }
}
